              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "activation_ids",
            "type": "PrPhaseId[]",
            "description": "Lease-holding activations, each mirrored by pr_phase timeline evidence."
          }
        ],
        "name": "PrCampaignState"
      },
      "text": [],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-gap-pr-series-shape": {
      "id": "b-gap-pr-series-shape",
      "type": "state-shape",
      "props": {
        "description": "Reviewable series state with durable feedback and validation evidence.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "work_items",
            "type": "PrWorkItem[]",
            "fields": [
              {
                "name": "summary",
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Compact operator-readable description of the feedback."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "last_validation",
            "type": "ValidationRecord",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Most recent gate validation for the series branch.",
            "fields": [
              {
                "name": "validated_at",
                "type": "timestamp"
              },
              {
                "name": "source_revision",
                "type": "SourceRevision"
              },
              {
                "name": "result",
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Validation outcome; publication requires the value clean."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "name": "PrSeriesState"
      },
      "text": [],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-why-the-campaign-is-most-17": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-why-the-campaign-is-most-17",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why the Campaign Is Mostly Dormant"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-upstream-review-usually-18": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-upstream-review-usually-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Upstream review usually takes much longer than local preparation or repair. Keeping the campaign durable but inactive preserves one review narrative without occupying the dispatch lease while the system waits for people or remote checks. A campaign normally runs to conclusion before the next run produces another batch, because overlapping campaigns would interleave learning and publication decisions from two baselines; runs during a campaign remain possible through explicit handoff, but are not the expected pattern."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-campaign-progress-19": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-campaign-progress-19",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Campaign Progress"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-campaign-state-names-whe-20": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-campaign-state-names-whe-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Campaign state names whether the durable review cycle is waiting, executing, or terminal:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-state-meaning-disp-21": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-state-meaning-disp-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "| State | Meaning | Dispatch Authority |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `preparing` | The campaign exists at its stable source anchor while prepared series and their validation evidence are assembled; nothing is open upstream. | No campaign lease is implied. |\n| `working` | An operator-entered activation is publishing, fixing, or validating series. | The campaign holds the dispatch lease. |\n| `in_review` | At least one series is open upstream and no activation holds the lease. | Only background remote observation and feedback ingestion may advance series. |\n| `completed` | Every series is merged or closed and the operator confirmed closure. | Terminal; the campaign cannot reacquire dispatch. |\n| `abandoned` | The operator ended the campaign without requiring every series to complete. | Terminal; unpublished evidence remains readable. |"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-operational-lifecycle-22": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-operational-lifecycle-22",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Operational Lifecycle"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-campaign-moves-throu-23": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-campaign-moves-throu-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The campaign moves through five operator-visible periods:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-operator-opens-a-cam-24": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-operator-opens-a-cam-24",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The operator opens a campaign from a stable point and records the prepared series in publication order. Legacy adoption is available only before a campaign exists; it creates the anchored campaign and imports matching split series in one operation."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-operator-activates-t-25": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-operator-activates-t-25",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The operator activates the campaign, which acquires the dispatch lease before any series is published, fixed, or validated."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-operator-confirms-th-26": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-operator-confirms-th-26",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The operator confirms the next publication batch, then releases the activation after all revision work and claimed feedback items have settled."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-campaign-stays-dorma-27": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-campaign-stays-dorma-27",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The campaign stays dormant during review while remote observation advances series and ingests feedback; the operator reactivates it when publication, repair, or validation is useful."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-operator-confirms-ca-28": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-operator-confirms-ca-28",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": true
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The operator confirms campaign closure after every series is merged or closed, or explicitly abandons the campaign when the remaining series will not proceed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-activations-and-timeline-29": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-activations-and-timeline-29",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Activations and Timeline Evidence"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-an-activation-is-the-lea-30": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-an-activation-is-the-lea-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "An activation is the lease-holding interval in which the campaign may mutate review workspaces or upstream series:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-acquisition-moves-the-ca-31": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-acquisition-moves-the-ca-31",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Acquisition moves the campaign into working state only after its campaign-specific dispatch lease is active."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-owning-session-recor-32": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-owning-session-recor-32",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The owning session records a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr_phase",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " timeline entry at lease acquisition and another at release, so every period of PR execution has durable boundaries."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-release-returns-the-camp-33": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-release-returns-the-camp-33",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Release returns the campaign to dormant review state and gives up dispatch only after no series is revising and no feedback work item remains in progress."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-publishing-fixer-execut-34": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-publishing-fixer-execut-34",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Publication verifies the active campaign lease before each remaining external call. Campaign work-item commands require the current lease identity and fence it to the campaign; QA repair verifies that ownership before and after execution."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-bounded-publication-35": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-bounded-publication-35",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Bounded Publication"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-publication-exposes-one-36": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-publication-exposes-one-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Publication exposes one operator-approved batch at a time so reviewers are never swamped:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-default-policy-selec-37": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-the-default-policy-selec-37",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The default policy selects four prepared series from the earliest unpublished batch; preparing later series does not publish them."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-every-publication-reques-38": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-every-publication-reques-38",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Every publication request requires explicit operator confirmation and an active campaign lease."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-a-series-must-carry-clea-39": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-a-series-must-carry-clea-39",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A series must carry clean validation against the campaign source anchor, and newer invalidation evidence blocks publication until the series is validated again."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-successful-publication-r-40": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-successful-publication-r-40",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Successful publication records the upstream identity on each series and advances only that confirmed batch into review."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-observation-and-feedback-41": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-observation-and-feedback-41",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Observation and Feedback"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-background-observation-c-42": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-background-observation-c-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Background observation changes durable review state without acquiring the dispatch lease:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-remote-review-evidence-a-43": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-remote-review-evidence-a-43",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Remote review evidence advances each published series independently to changes requested, approved, merged, or closed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-feedback-is-ingested-imm-44": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-feedback-is-ingested-imm-44",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Feedback is ingested immediately as deduplicated pending work items, and its owning series reflects that work even while another workflow holds dispatch."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-observation-never-claims-45": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-observation-never-claims-45",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Observation never claims a feedback item or mutates a checkout, so evidence can remain current without starting fixer execution."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-fixer-work-begins-only-i-46": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-fixer-work-begins-only-i-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Fixer work begins only inside an activation, which keeps evidence intake separate from execution:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-claiming-pending-work-mo-47": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-claiming-pending-work-mo-47",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Claiming pending work moves both the item to in progress and its series to revising under one durable transition."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-resolving-work-records-t-48": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-resolving-work-records-t-48",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Resolving work records that each item was addressed by a pushed revision or by an answer in the review thread before returning the series to published review state. Resolved work items are terminal and cannot be claimed again."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-an-activation-cannot-rel-49": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-an-activation-cannot-rel-49",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "An activation cannot release while a series is revising or any campaign work item remains in progress."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-gap-pr-workitem-statuses": {
      "id": "b-gap-pr-workitem-statuses",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Status",
          "Meaning",
          "Terminal"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "resolved",
            "The feedback was addressed by a pushed revision or answered in the review thread.",
            "yes"
          ],
          [
            "declined",
            "The feedback was deliberately not actioned and carries a reason.",
            "yes"
          ]
        ],
        "title": "PR work-item terminal outcomes"
      },
      "text": [],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-series-progress-50": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-series-progress-50",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Series Progress"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-series-state-separates-l-51": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-series-state-separates-l-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Series state separates local readiness, remote review, and terminal outcome so each source of evidence has one place to advance it:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-state-meaning-adva-52": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-state-meaning-adva-52",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "| State | Meaning | Advanced By |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `prepared` | The series is locally cut and gate-validated but is not open upstream. | A lease-holding activation |\n| `published` | The series is open upstream and waiting for review. | An operator-confirmed publication batch |\n| `changes_requested` | Review feedback exists as pending work. | Background observation or feedback ingestion |\n| `revising` | Fixers own feedback work and may mutate the series workspace. | A lease-holding activation |\n| `approved` | Remote review approved the series and merge is pending. | Background observation |\n| `merged` | Upstream merged the series. Terminal. | Background observation |\n| `closed` | The series was withdrawn or rejected without merging. Terminal. | Background observation or an explicit operator close |"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-legacy-series-adoption-53": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-legacy-series-adoption-53",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Legacy Series Adoption"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-legacy-split-pr-records-54": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-legacy-split-pr-records-54",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Legacy split-PR records remain usable through a pre-campaign adoption command that creates and activates the anchored durable campaign before importing them:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-adoption-recognizes-the-55": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-adoption-recognizes-the-55",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Adoption recognizes the existing split-series branches and converts their observed local and upstream state into campaign series without republishing them."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-existing-order-manifest-56": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-existing-order-manifest-56",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Existing order, manifests, validation evidence, and review outcomes determine batch placement and current series state; a changes-requested record also becomes pending feedback work."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-repeating-adoption-skips-57": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-repeating-adoption-skips-57",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Repeating the adoption route for the deterministic anchored campaign returns the existing result, so retries do not duplicate durable review objects."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-campaign-closure-58": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-campaign-closure-58",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Campaign Closure"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-campaign-closure-is-an-o-59": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-campaign-closure-is-an-o-59",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Campaign closure is an operator-confirmed terminal decision rather than an automatic consequence of remote status:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-completion-is-available-60": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-completion-is-available-60",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Completion is available only when every series is merged or closed, and the closure record preserves the final outcome of every series."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-a-working-campaign-relea-61": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-a-working-campaign-relea-61",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A working campaign releases its activation before it completes, leaving matching acquisition and release boundaries in the session timeline."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-abandonment-is-the-expli-62": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-abandonment-is-the-expli-62",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Abandonment is the explicit terminal path when the operator decides unpublished or unresolved series will not continue."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-a-completed-or-abandoned-63": {
      "id": "b-20-operator-flow-and-pr-tracking-a-completed-or-abandoned-63",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A completed or abandoned campaign remains readable as review evidence and cannot publish or revise another series."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
}
